= The Collectivist Memo

With the call for fresh elections, someone in the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> apparatus let a circular reach some of our friends in our Left.

The news is out that Halsmark has pushed for electoral abstentionism. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> will not enter a national government of the Commonwealth, will not support one from outside, and will not treat the difference between a <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marcher**</span> ministry and a propertied one, despite the near-electoral certainty that we will emerge the largest party.

The internal memo notes heavy objection from the smaller Conciliators faction, who advocate for parliamentary participation and a larger united front with the  <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> noting that refusal to participate in a stable republic is dooming the Collectivist cause. The Collectivists at large were not convinced, and the position has been sidelined.

Our reading of internal <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> politics comes largely from educated guesses. Those of us who keep a line open to the <span style="color: #D50000;">Collectivist International</span> hear a great deal more, and a few within our leadership have connections to some higher-up <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> still, but unless we make a heavy effort to reach out to them, it is unlikely that Halsmark's faction will ever lose its prominence.

- @intransigent
- @see_the_light

@intransigent
title: The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> are as intransigent as ever.

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> still do not understand that the Commonwealth, flaws and all, is still worth protecting. Some grassroots chapters will remain friendlier, and electoral cooperation there is possible, but unless Collectivist leadership changes or relations warm drastically, it is unlikely that our more radical <span style="color: #c00000;">**Reformist**</span> cousins will come to reason.

@see_the_light
title: If only they could see the light.
on-arrival: left_strength += 2; reformist_strength -= 2 if reformist_strength >= 2

Many of our grassroot members are close with individual <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and our own  <span style="color: #c00000;">Left</span> agree broadly that the major pushback from the Conciliators is definitive evidence that the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> would be our closest ally if we can gain their trust. 

The broad leadership of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is unconvinced. It may take the efforts of a few of our more sympathetic leaders if proper outreach is to happen without significant circumstantial changes in the Commonwealth.
